    "feed": "005 backfills existing inbox IDs and allocates AUTOINCREMENT arrivals only on INSERT. Same-ID UPDATE/ACK/read/refinement creates no arrival. Deleted rows cascade, and sqlite_sequence survives clear/retention. A synthetic sequence greater than 2^53 is returned exactly as a decimal string.",
    "baselineAndScope": "Missing cursor or changed runtime/source scope/Shanghai day silently moves to the current high watermark. Exact fields and decimal/i64 syntax are validated first. Only current-domain sequence ahead of the high watermark is rejected; a valid older-runtime larger sequence safely baselines.",
    "promptConsumption": "Every arrival through the read high watermark is consumed once, including future/invalid/other-day/expired/ineligible/overflow. Selected prompts are bounded to8 with alerts before completion, parsed-time descending and stable-ID ascending. A previously future timestamp becoming current and unknown->completed refinement do not replay.",
    "boolAndOutcomeSemantics": "notifyEligible and animationAcknowledged require actual JSON boolean true, not numeric1. Read/notified do not grant or suppress animation eligibility. Case-insensitive completed/success/succeeded/normal/ok align with the existing success set; done remains an alert.",
    "clockAndHealth": "Chrono RFC3339 parsing and Shanghai day are used directly. Existing active-root/uncertain freshness uses signed integer seconds in[-5,600), invalid/future/stale remain uncertain; child turns do not inflate roots. Missing successful scan/event watermarks remain null; failed reads do not return zeros or increment revision. Health issues is grouped(kind,message) count, conflicts unresolved count.",
    "details": "Request is bound to current day/runtime/source fingerprint and rejects unknown query fields. Native scalar traversal excludes aliases/excluded facts and invalid/missing totals, never adds legacy/aggregate estimates, preserves empty null vs recorded zero, and computes cache rate only from valid input/cacheRead pairs. Latest TTFT uses completedAt??startedAt ordering with stable lastEventAt/physical-order ties; latest null is retained. Completed-at Shanghai midnight with an explicit offset is tested.",
    "clearTransaction": "A controlled BEFORE INSERT settings trigger aborts inboxWatermark update during clear_inbox. The production action returns Err and inbox data, feed rows and sequence remain intact; removing the owned obstruction permits successful atomic clear and strictly later arrivals. clear_data also preserves the high watermark and establishes a fresh scope.",
    "migrationFailure": "A self-created existing-v4 fixture contains inbox facts. Backfill preserves payloads, updates do not allocate arrivals, and reopen is idempotent. A deliberate final trigger-name collision makes Core::open fail; version4 and old data remain, feed DDL/backfill roll back, the pre-v5 backup is readable, and removing only the authored obstruction in its copy permits recovery."
  },
